silient. Policy is no longer providing active lift (balance sheet contraction), but financial conditions are loose enough to support equities if macro doesn't deteriorate further. The tightening in both labour and inflation metrics creates tactical headwind, but not yet a structural reversal. This is a consolidation after a move—support from risk appetite and loose financial conditions, headwind from collapsing positioning and inflating inflation, with breadth confirming the slowdown is real. A narrow long is warranted, sized to the genuine uncertainty in this configuration.", "drivers": "[
